- Finish retiring imgui/: decide whether any of its remaining files (poc.js,
  imgui-debugger.js, target.js, ...) are still worth keeping now that gui/ covers the
  supported GUI mode, and remove the rest.

- gui/ parity extras (gui/PLAN.md phase 5 leftovers beyond what's landed): full REPL
  command parity in the console pane's command line (completion, history) matching the
  terminal REPL.

- watch: software watchpoints step with `next`, so a change made inside a called function shows up when it returns;
  an engine-side data watch would be exact and fast.
- return/jump: the engine protocol has no forced return, so `return` is missing; needs a protocol request.
- server mode: replay the current state (entry stop, stack) to a client connecting late.
- batch mode: `source FILE` command and `define`, if scripts start to need them.
